		text = "When the Head acts on a Taboo, it doesn't stop at the guilty. It removes everything connected: the workshop, the records, the sign over the door, sometimes the whole block. Neighbors wake up and can't remember who lived upstairs. The mailbox has no name on it, and never did.\n\nAlmost nobody remembers. That is the point. A few people do, for reasons no one understands, and they learn quickly not to say so.\n\nIf you remember someone the City says never existed, keep it to yourself. The Head is thorough, and it checks its work.",
