		category = "terms",
		title = "The Knock at 3:13",
		text = "Every Backstreets child hears this story eventually. Some time after 3:13, someone knocks on your door, three soft taps, and a voice you know asks to be let in. Your mother. Your best friend. Your own voice, from when you were small.\n\nThe Sweepers can't come into a locked home; that's the Head's own law. So, the story goes, the things that walk with them have learned to ask.\n\nNobody knows whether it's true. Everybody keeps the rule anyway: whoever is knocking, whatever they say, you don't open the door until the third wave has passed.",
