		text = "You can't fight the Sweepers. Everyone who tried is part of the reason the streets are so clean in the morning. So the Backstreets has other ideas, most of them bad.\n\nShopkeepers who lift a shutter a hand's width at 3:10 and name a price. Old women selling brass tokens that make the waves \"pass you by\". Drains, lift shafts, rooftops, the backs of delivery vans. Some of it works. Most of it works once.\n\nThe only bargain that always works is the oldest one: be home before three, and lock the door.",
