		text = "Every morning after the Night, the notice boards in the Backstreets get a fresh sheet of paper: the names of people who didn't come home. Some Districts print them. Some just pin up handwritten scraps.\n\nNobody reads the list in front of anyone else. You read it quickly, the way you'd touch a hot stove, and then you go to work.\n\nFixers read the lists too, for different reasons. The same kind of name turning up three mornings running, on the same street, means somebody is doing this on purpose.",
