		title = "Number Nine, Bellhouse Row",
		secret = true,
		text = "On paper, Number Nine is a five-floor tenement with cheap rent and a broken lift. In person it has as many floors as it wants. The stairs count differently at night. People who go past the fourth-floor landing come down days later, or not at all.\n\nLimbus Company would call it a Location-type Distortion: a whole place bent out of shape by someone's despair, with an Inflection Point hidden somewhere inside that started it all. Nobody who went looking for it came back to say.\n\nThe strangest part is the address. Number Nine isn't always on Bellhouse Row.",
